       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release).\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is well above the typical maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended orders include:\n- 500 mg three times daily\n- 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg twice daily\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses (for example 850 mg twice daily)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
